roduces an  awful lot more vocabulary lots there's  20 chapters  uh i guess two or so of them are  recapitulare which means to um  to review  but other than that each one of them  introduces at least 20 or so new items  of vocabulary  that's good  the other thing that's good is that they  introduce different aspects of the  grammar with lots of examples so rather  than just explanations they'll have a an  introduction and then they have lots of  examples  and so i find it very useful to read  these examples i don't know whether they  stick or don't stick i mean you have to  read these things over and over again  i'm reading the book now for about the  third or fourth  time reading some of the same examples  reading the dialogues going over the  vocabulary list all those things so to  that extent i'm willing to spend more  time on on teach yourself  than on pimster because at any rate if i  have dedicated time i'm going to read  i'm not going to listen that's just how  i learn  uh plus i took the cd from the pimsleur  and i've listened to it a few times now  some of the dialogues are still a bit of  a blur  the disadvantage oh and one thing that i  don't like about teach yourself is that  there is a fair amount of english  button they don't  similar to pimpster but the big  difference between pimsleur and teach  yourself is  that teach yourself the sound is not as  clear  the clearest sound on the teach yourself  is the british guy who's explaining  stuff to you  some of the romanian speakers are clear  some are quite unclear  some of the dialogues have you you're  supposed supposedly it's a phone call so  you hear the phone dial  and one of the voices is kind of  obscured because it's coming out of a  telephone so they do things to make the  sound less clear  plus some of the voices are not clear  and i experienced this with my czech  teacher self they had one voice there  that was so soft and unclear it was  too annoying to listen to the big  advantage of pimpster 